A population cartogram of the United States rendered in Piet Mondrian's signature style, with rectangular blocks of primary red, blue, and soft purple arranged in varying sizes to represent population density, separated by bold black grid lines of different thicknesses, the blocks flowing and merging where colors blend into lavender and violet tones, creating an abstract geometric composition that suggests unity within apparent division, the familiar shape of America barely recognizable yet emotionally present, warm yellow accents scattered throughout like points of light, the entire composition balanced asymmetrically in true De Stijl fashion against a cream white background
